Attribution — Android Open Source Project
================================================================================

Inspector Widget is a clean-room reimplementation of Android Studio's Layout
Inspector. Its on-device agent, wire protocol, and inspection techniques were
reverse-engineered from and modeled on the following Android Open Source Project
(AOSP) components, each itself licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  * Android Studio / tools-base — the Layout Inspector (the dynamic-layout-
    inspector, ui-inspector, and app-inspection on-device agents): typed
    view-property extraction via the framework InspectionCompanion SPI, the
    deflated-BITMAP screenshot wire format (BitmapUtils), and the agent
    injection / message-framing layering.
    https://android.googlesource.com/platform/tools/base/

  * Jetpack Compose / AndroidX — androidx.compose.ui.tooling.data (the slot-table
    reader used to recover the composable hierarchy, parameters, modifiers, and
    file:line source positions), androidx.compose.ui semantics, and the inspector
    enablement path (isDebugInspectorInfoEnabled, HotReloader).
    https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/

  * The Android framework runtime APIs used on-device: android.view.ViewDebug
    rendering-command (SKP) capture, PixelCopy, the accessibility node APIs, and
    JVMTI agent attachment.
    https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/

No source code from these projects is copied into or redistributed by this
repository; they are credited as the basis for the reverse-engineered design. At
runtime the inspector reflects against the target application's own bundled
AndroidX libraries, and it downloads Google's "skiaparser" tool from the public
Android SDK repository on demand — neither is vendored here.

